you had Carson Palmer—

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:10.917
- Listen.
- A Heisman Trophy winner.

00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:13.000
- Look where I—
- That doesn't matter!
- I was in Cincinnati.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.667
You played for the 49ers!
- That has nothin' to do with it!

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:17.708
- The Cowboys, the Eagles—
- They weren't that good,
the 49ers, though.

00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:19.375
- Wait a minute!
- The 49ers weren't that good.

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:21.375
- These are awesome
organizations.

00:01:21.375 --> 00:01:23.458
When I came in,
I was in the s--t bowl

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:25.292
according to everybody else.
- Whoa!

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:27.083
- And I made the most of the cards
that I was dealt.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:28.792
- Bro, I could've played
for the Cleveland Browns

00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:30.250
and did what I did—
- So basically—

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.667
-So don't tell me—
- I'm not finished talking.

00:01:31.667 --> 00:01:33.833
- I played with the Buffalo Bills—
- I'm not finished talking.
— And got off.

00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:37.167
- I'm not finished talking.
- I played with the Cincinnati
Bengals with you and got off. - OK, Jesus f--king Christ.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.958
- Was there one part
of the game

00:01:38.958 --> 00:01:41.083
any part of the game
that you stole from each other

00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:42.667
where you were like, damn—
- I couldn't.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.375
I couldn't do anything
he did, honestly.
- No?

00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:47.625
- His DNA, his makeup,
his skill set is completely—

00:01:47.625 --> 00:01:50.167
I mean, night and day,
completely.

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.083
The stuff he would do,
the stiff-arming people

00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:53.417
never f--kin' worked.

00:01:53.417 --> 00:01:55.125
I would go the opposite way
- [Laughing]

00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:57.375
- Cuz I was more of
a finesse player.

00:01:57.375 --> 00:01:59.583
My favorite thing
to watch T.O. do

00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:01.125
him and Brandon Marshall

00:02:01.125 --> 00:02:02.583
dudes playin' bump-and-run.

00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:04.833
Let's say I'm tired—
fourth quarter.

00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:07.833
They have this f--kin'
tug-and-pull where they invite

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:11.042
the contact and wait for you
to get a hold and pull by.

00:02:11.042 --> 00:02:13.708
How in the f--k?
- Yeah, I know. I've seen it.

00:02:13.708 --> 00:02:15.708
- I tried it in practice
one time.

00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:18.125
I'm right there in the
same spot. Can't get off.

00:02:18.125 --> 00:02:19.875
- So, you're on the Bengals.

00:02:19.875 --> 00:02:23.125
What was the day
when he joined the Bengals?

00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:26.708
- I had lobbied for that big-time
with Marvin, with Marvin.

00:02:26.708 --> 00:02:29.500
I said—I asked Marvin,
you know, a lot, man.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.042
"We really need to bring T in.

00:02:31.042 --> 00:02:33.875
I think it would help us
offensively tremendously."

00:02:33.875 --> 00:02:36.333
- Who was your receiver coach,
God bless his soul, that year?

00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:38.375
- Sheppard, Mike Sheppard.
- Mike Sheppard at the time.

00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:40.750
- Dealing with you two in
meetings must've been amazing.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.375
I would've loved to have been in
a meeting with you two.
- Nah, it was easy.

00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:44.625
When I'm workin', I'm locked in.

00:02:44.625 --> 00:02:46.708
- Yeah, I know you are.
I know you both are.

00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.208
- Yeah, I mean, again,
people may think

00:02:49.208 --> 00:02:52.125
that we're uncoachable
based on the antics

00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:55.042
and how we, you know, go about,
but when it came to football

00:02:55.042 --> 00:02:57.000
like, literally—
- That's what nobody gets to see.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.667
- Right, I know.
- In the workplace, when it's time to work.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.583
I remember he's tryin'
to get me to slow down

00:03:01.583 --> 00:03:02.875
on Fridays, remember?

00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:04.792
- Yeah.
- Man, Fridays.

00:03:04.792 --> 00:03:06.042
Man, I'm out there balls to the wall.

00:03:06.042 --> 00:03:07.458
- You know how Fridays are,
you know?

00:03:07.458 --> 00:03:09.083
- It's a chill day.
- It's time to taper down.

00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:10.750
- I know you were. I know. Right.
- Man, listen.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.208
- I'm like, "Dude."

00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:14.083
- T was like,
"What are you doin'?"

00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:15.958
I'm takin' scout team—
- Yeah, I'm like, "Bro!"

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:19.167
- And this is well into
my 10th, ninth year.

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.500
I'm just out there movin'.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.833
- Yeah, the perception is wrong.

00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:23.000
- I remember just—

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.500
I'm just growin' up. Think about the
Hurricanes in the '90s.

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.000
- Yeah.
- And that's what I grew up

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.792
watching, so as
a kid growing up

00:03:27.792 --> 00:03:30.042
the game of football
was about having fun.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:33.792
When you're in the NFL and you
misbehave or they do something

00:03:33.792 --> 00:03:35.625
you don't like or you
don't follow their rules

00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:37.250
what's the first thing
they take from you?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:38.875
- Money.
- Money.

00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:40.750
- Money. Because that's what
they think you value the most.
- Right.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:43.458
- But for me, the money was gonna come.
- Regardless.
- Money comes and goes.

00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:45.917
It's gonna come regardless,
which is why I never stopped

00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:48.000
doin' what I was doin'
because the money was great.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.625
It was awesome. But when I didn't
have any money, this is the way

00:03:50.625 --> 00:03:53.583
I played the game of football,
which is why I never stopped.

00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:55.208
- Even with—and
to go a step further

00:03:55.208 --> 00:03:56.833
you talk about the Hall of Fame

00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:59.000
and everybody realizes
when you're in the Hall of Fame

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.958
obviously, there are
financial opportunities

00:04:01.958 --> 00:04:05.750
well outside of that,
and so I was well aware of that

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.833
and I had some Hall of Famers
even told me—they was like

00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:10.167
"Man, you gonna mess up
these opportunities."

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.375
You know, for me,
I'm just like Chad, you know?

00:04:12.375 --> 00:04:14.292
Money comes and goes.

00:04:14.292 --> 00:04:18.000
If I had to, you know,
if I'm put in a situation

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.000
where I gotta choose money
over my family and friends

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.333
I'mma choose my family
and friends all day.

00:04:23.333 --> 00:04:26.208
And it was just, it was
sad to see how

00:04:26.208 --> 00:04:27.958
the media, again,
they didn't allow themselves

00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:31.000
an opportunity to know
who we are as people

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.125
and they went
into the perception

00:04:33.125 --> 00:04:34.375
of who they thought we were

00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:36.000
and again, we
just went out there

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.792
and we just had fun
with the game.

00:04:37.792 --> 00:04:39.833
- It makes it more interesting
to have the villains

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.708
to have someone to talk about.
There has to be a bad guy.

00:04:41.708 --> 00:04:45.500
- There has to be.
- They have to, but it's unfair, like you said

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:50.208
because, again, how can you
justify Tom Brady doin'

00:04:50.208 --> 00:04:53.333
or sayin' some of the same
things that I've done—

00:04:53.333 --> 00:04:55.000
- Right.
- Showing emotion.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.667
- Right, yelling the
F-word at the stands.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.875
- Right. Exactly.
I've seen him curse out coaches.

00:04:58.875 --> 00:05:01.167
I've seen him berate his own teammates.
- Yeah, right.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:05.917
- But he's looked at and upon as
a leader, a champion, you know?

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:08.500
- You know what,
if I had to do it again

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.417
honestly, to restart
and had to do it again

00:05:10.417 --> 00:05:12.750
I'd do it the exact same way.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:14.250
I wouldn't change s--t.

